            title = "The Train Station Chess Club",
            tagline = "A group of commuters and students create a welcoming chess corner built on patience, fair play, and shared learning.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "The Folding Table", listOf("At the small station waiting room, a folding table stood unused beside the noticeboard. A station volunteer suggested turning it into a chess corner during the supervised afternoon community hour.", "Yusuf, who had learned chess from his aunt, offered to bring a spare set. The station manager approved a trial, with clear rules about keeping walkways open and packing away before the room closed.", "The first meeting attracted only three people, but they played two cheerful games.")),
                StoryPart(2, "The Missing Knight", listOf("The next week, the group discovered that one knight was missing from the chess set. They checked the storage box and the sign-out sheet before assuming someone had taken it.", "A cleaner found the piece in the side pocket of the set's cloth bag. The group added a quick inventory check to its closing routine.", "Yusuf suggested drawing a picture of the complete set on the box so younger players could help check it.")),
                StoryPart(3, "A Beginner's Board", listOf("A student named Feyi wanted to join but did not know how the pieces moved. Yusuf offered to teach one piece at a time, beginning with the rook and bishop.", "They used a demonstration board and played short practice turns. Feyi asked questions whenever a move seemed confusing.", "The group decided to keep a beginner board available at every session, so new players would not feel they had interrupted a game.")),
                StoryPart(4, "The Quiet Rule", listOf("One afternoon, two experienced players argued over a move. Their voices grew loud enough to disturb people waiting for trains.", "The volunteer paused the game and reminded everyone of the club's agreement: explain disagreements calmly, check the rules, and accept the result of a fair review.", "The players checked the rulebook and continued. They later helped write a short fair-play guide for the table.")),
                StoryPart(5, "A Tournament Idea", listOf("The group proposed a friendly mini-tournament for the end of the month. The station manager agreed on the condition that it remain small and never block passenger information or access.", "Yusuf helped make a schedule that allowed players to leave whenever their train was announced. No one would be penalised for missing a round because they had to travel.", "The tournament was designed to make the station feel welcoming, not to create pressure.")),
                StoryPart(6, "The Unusual Opening", listOf("Feyi surprised the group by trying an opening she had learned from a library book. She explained that she had practised it with a paper board at home.", "Yusuf asked her to show the idea slowly. The others discussed possible responses, and Feyi learned that a plan could be interesting even when it did not guarantee a win.", "The group added a shelf of chess books and printed beginner puzzles donated by the library.")),
                StoryPart(7, "A Delayed Train", listOf("A service delay brought more people into the waiting room than usual. The chess club moved its table closer to the wall and paused play whenever staff needed the space.", "A commuter asked whether she could join a quick game. Feyi welcomed her and explained the beginner board.", "The game lasted only a few minutes before the train arrived, but the commuter promised to return on another afternoon.")),
                StoryPart(8, "The Tournament Day", listOf("On tournament day, the players signed up with first names only. The volunteer explained the schedule and reminded everyone that travel announcements came first.", "The rounds were short and friendly. Feyi won one game, lost another, and drew a third after both players recognised a repeated position.", "The group celebrated the draw as carefully as the wins. Everyone had learned something.")),
                StoryPart(9, "A New Clock", listOf("A local shop donated a chess clock after the club explained how it would be used. The players read its instructions together and agreed that beginners could choose games without a timer.", "The station manager asked the group to keep the clock stored with the board and to report any missing equipment at closing.", "The club's small equipment list now included the clock, the pieces, two boards, and the rulebook.")),
                StoryPart(10, "One More Move", listOf("The station chess corner became a regular feature of the supervised community hour. A notice invited beginners, experienced players, and anyone who simply wanted to watch and learn.", "Yusuf gave the first spare set to Feyi, who helped teach the next newcomer. The club kept the original set at the station for shared games.", "When the final train announcement sounded, the players packed the pieces away together. There was always another game waiting for the next meeting."))
            )
        )
    )
